00:32:53.890 --> 00:33:03.130
Anubhav Kokane: We are using OAuth2 authorization code flow with Pixi. It is the industry standard for public clients, and

171
00:33:03.320 --> 00:33:07.510
Anubhav Kokane: It helps protect against the authorization code interception.

172
00:33:08.150 --> 00:33:21.390
Anubhav Kokane: We use JSON web tokens for stateless authorization, which means that server does not need to Maintain.

173
00:33:21.790 --> 00:33:23.250
Anubhav Kokane: Session state.

174
00:33:23.490 --> 00:33:26.619
Anubhav Kokane: We have also implemented role-based

175
00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:32.120
Anubhav Kokane: Access control, which means a user's role will determine his access permissions.

176
00:33:32.800 --> 00:33:37.850
Anubhav Kokane: All these tokens are generated server-side with strong cryptographic sign.

177
00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:40.990
Anubhav Kokane: In Cloud Fair Workers.

178
00:33:41.470 --> 00:33:48.080
Anubhav Kokane: Now, moving to, now let's take a deep dive at JSON Web Token.

179
00:33:48.430 --> 00:33:55.189
Anubhav Kokane: So, the JSON web token is divided into three parts, a header, which determines the algorithm.

180
00:33:55.310 --> 00:34:02.569
Anubhav Kokane: A payload, which contains the details of user's identity and role. And finally, a signature.

181
00:34:03.050 --> 00:34:06.699
Anubhav Kokane: Which helps ensure the token has not been tampered with.

182
00:34:07.560 --> 00:34:14.819
Anubhav Kokane: We use strong cryptographic signing algorithms, HS256 and, RS256.

183
00:34:15.560 --> 00:34:17.640
Anubhav Kokane: Depending upon the use case.

184
00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:21.060
Anubhav Kokane: aren't…

